    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261-a4">

                <pb facs="0479" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg379"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    896.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fernandez to Mr.
                            H. H. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 3,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have had the honor to
                    receive his excellency Mr. Morgan’s note which he addressed to this department
                    under date of August 26 last, referring to the case of Mr. Howard C. Walker.</p>
                <p>In my note of the 28th of May of this year I informed Mr. Morgan that it did not
                    appear on the register of matriculation that the said Walker was a citizen of
                    the United States and that this circumstance prevented my accepting the ulterior
                    official intervention of his excellency in the premises.</p>
                <p>In calling your attention, although with regret, to my statement referred to I
                    renew to you the assurances of my attentive consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSÉ FERNANDEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
